{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1782060076,"nonce":"Tr+kLSYqv7xKBxkmkCs3gaspgDQ=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABGM8t_g","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/305","origin":"github"},"title":"Revise sidescan grazing_deg default 62.5° → ~35° (field-measured; #303 follow-up)","message":"## Summary\n\nRevise the SideVü side-scan **grazing tilt default** in `bizzyboat_project11/urdf/sensors/sidescan.xacro` from the shipped `grazing_deg=62.5°` (half-fan-off-nadir, #303) to **~35°**, the value measured from field bag data.\n\nPart of #185.\n\n## Why\n\n#303 set `grazing_deg=62.5°` from a geometric \"half-fan off nadir\" argument (90 − 55/2). A subsequent offline analysis of field sonar bags (2026-06-21) shows that's **~27° too steep** — it's a tiling heuristic, not how a side-imaging sonar is actually aimed.\n\n**Measured boresight depression ≈ 35°**, converging across:\n- **Raw I(φ) angular-profile peak ~38°** (port ~42° / stbd ~33°; the split is a static vessel list), consistent across 5 days and 30/35/50 m range settings, two independent depth sources (`nadir_depth` + a peak-anchored ClearVü down-channel pick validated to −0.08 m).\n- **Minus the near-nadir backscatter steep-bias → true boresight ~35°.**\n- **Roll regression** (using a day with vessel roll) validated the geometry: per-ping steep-edge vs roll gave **opposite-sign slopes ≈ ±1** for port vs starboard, exactly as the beam geometry predicts; roll-removed intercepts 31–39°.\n- **Patent corroboration**: recreational side-imaging (Garmin/Humminbird/Navico) fires ~20–40°, nominal ~30° below horizontal (US7652952B2, US11137495B2). Survey towfish ~10°.\n\n**Method** is TVG-independent: the steepest fan edge sets the shortest slant range to bottom, `sin(θ_steepest)=h/R_side_first`, `boresight=θ_steepest−27.5°`. First-return is a time-of-arrival pick, so gain/TVG don't move it.\n\n## Limitation (documented, not blocking)\n\nThe fan-width / shallow −3 dB edge could not be *cleanly* resolved — at 30/35 m range it's beyond the window; at 50 m it's right at the ~10° window floor (soft-consistent with the 55° spec, span ~58°, midpoint ~39°). A clean fan-width check would need a 50–60 m-range pass over 10–15 m water with a reliable depth channel (possible future capture). This does not affect the boresight result.\n\n## Change\n\n- `grazing_deg` default `62.5` → `35` in the `garmin_sidescan` macro.\n- Rewrite the header rationale: replace the half-fan-off-nadir derivation with the measured ~35° (+ patent ~30° corroboration, + backscatter steep-bias note). Keep the param overridable for calibration.\n\nOne file, ~1 value + comments.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}